{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020657-allowing-definite-but-finite-victories-against-pentex","id":1020657,"title":"Allowing Definite, but finite victories against pentex.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T14:41:21-08:00","id":1020657,"title":"Allowing Definite, but finite victories against pentex.","content":"one problem I , and I suspect a lot of other ST's have, is using pentex as a managable villain, to k eep the game worthwhile... the PC's have to be able to make gains against them, to keep them in the game, they need to be able to adapt.<br /> <br /> I recently thought the new movie &quot;the thinning&quot; Might be a good example for that any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T18:16:40-08:00","id":1020740,"title":"","content":"No, I'm fairly certain that The Thinning would just be a human society's attempts to eliminate people considered undesirable and support the wealthy elite's control of culture. After all, an aptitude test is based heavily on social position and wealth, which contribute to better education, and not about very much intrinsic to any given individual (being sharp is mostly not inherited, but the result of environmental nurturing, down to what food you eat and in what quantity). Actual victories against Pentex would be in introducing the concept that corporate-driven capitalism is unnecessary for existence, not a setup that's more eugenics fail covering up even worse shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-21-2016, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T18:52:47-08:00","id":1020750,"title":"","content":"I would suggest looking at the Brazilian science fiction TV show '3%' on Netflix for something that would be more egalitarian (if horrific in a different way) than the Thinning. Anyway, back to the topic, I definitely think that the Garou should consistently have substantial victories against Pentex, but we are talking about a company that probably controls 5% of global GDP (which would mean that they would have revenues of $3.5 trillion per year). If you assume the normal profitability for corporations of 10% of revenues, they would have profits of $350 billion per year.<br /> <br /> The Garou could be killing a subsidiary the size of AT&amp;T every year, and they probably do, but Pentex can just take the loss as a write-off on their overall profits. The Amazon War was just a side project for Pentex, something to mess up the entire war, but they were not losing substantial amounts of money over it. I doubt that they spent more than $30 billion a year on the Amazon War, less than 1% of their revenue, but that was probably enough to send 150,000 fomori a year into the Amazon (probably 20 fomori a year for every Fera living in the Amazon). I wonder if they wrote it off as research and development costs on their taxes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T19:00:15-08:00","id":1020752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020657-allowing-definite-but-finite-victories-against-pentex?p=1020740#post1020740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm fairly certain that The Thinning would just be a human society's attempts to eliminate people considered undesirable and support the wealthy elite's control of culture. After all, an aptitude test is based heavily on social position and wealth, which contribute to better education, and not about very much intrinsic to any given individual (being sharp is mostly not inherited, but the result of environmental nurturing, down to what food you eat and in what quantity). Actual victories against Pentex would be in introducing the concept that corporate-driven capitalism is unnecessary for existence, not a setup that's more eugenics fail covering up even worse shit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> my comparison was in the end of that movie, the bad guys get embarassed substantialy, and are forced to stop rigging the aptitude tests as much.<br /> <br /> <br /> but the system while under a lot more scrutiny, endures.<br /> <br /> and is worse then the public knows.<br /> <br /> the children who fail arent just euthanized their used as slave labor.<br /> <br /> And I wanted to say if you found evidence that a local pentex subsidiary was involved in this or that impropriety, like say Magadon got caught illegally using Stem cells collected from aborted fetuses, or such think their response would be like the governers was at the end of the movie &quot;I am surprised and appalled...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T19:07:09-08:00","id":1020755,"title":"","content":"If you restate the problem, it is a common one a lot of GMs have: how do you have a recurring antagonist that can constantly fight the PCs, without the PCs becoming frustrated because they are unable (or never allowed to by the GM) to defeat him?<br /> <br /> One of the solutions it to keep the actual villain offstage while his minions work on various projects that the PCs can thwart. With PENTEX it is actually easier as the Directors shouldn't be attacking the PCs directly. They always have minions instead. So come up with some very specific projects/goals that PENTEX wants to accomplish. Select one of the subsidiaries to be responsible for doing it. Come up with an intermediary leader who can direct the project, but which is utterly expendable if the PCs just kill him. The PCs can then go about defeating that project/plan, yet PENTEX itself is still around. If the players don't feel that it seems like a win, be sure you somehow document the cost of their actions to PENTEX so they can see real money, power, assets, etc. be lost and not replaced. Perhaps mention a second future project that is now cancelled as a result of the losses from the PCs.<br /> <br /> Another option is to completely sacrifice one of the less important subsidiaries in your campaign. Maybe you feel that Endron International or O'Tolleys should be too big for the PCs to take down, but what about video game designer Tellus Enterprises (the video game and computer industry is notorious for new companies achieving dominance out of nowhere, and old ones losing marketshare and going backrupt) or Autumn Health Management Systems? Make that one of the prime threats in your chronicle. Think of a few nefarious things they do that you feel the PCs want to stop, come up with a few NPC villains, informers, moles, heavies, etc.; then have the PCs come across them; and then let them do whatever plan they want - and if it is good enough, permanently eliminate that subsidiary from your chronicle.<br /> <br /> Lastly, maybe in all of this there is one big bad guy among the Directors who've been hurt the most by this and the PCs have learned by name. At some point after they gain enough experience and knowledge, allow them to bump him off at the climax of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> PENTEX will still be around and quite powerful, but the PCs will have dealt them an obvious setback and should have a sense of accomplisment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T19:11:28-08:00","id":1020756,"title":"","content":"Pentex has often been referred to as a hydra. Even if you have defeat it in one area, it's likely to be making progress in another. So your group manages to shut down the Endron refinery that's pumping toxic chemicals into the ground water, O'Tolley's has opened up 2 more restaurants, Magadon just made a deal with Wal-greens is now the back-end supplier for half the pharmaceuticals in town, and investors tied to King Breweries recently obtained licenses to construct a massive, three-story alcohol warehouse store.<br /> <br /> Pentex has so many heads - so many fronts - it's honestly very easy to get a victory against them. But at the same time, it's hard to make those victories meaningful because even if you push one group out of business, five more are still making huge gains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:36:00-08:00","id":1023316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020657-allowing-definite-but-finite-victories-against-pentex?p=1020755#post1020755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the solutions it to keep the actual villain offstage while his minions work on various projects that the PCs can thwart. With PENTEX it is actually easier as the Directors shouldn't be attacking the PCs directly. They always have minions instead. So come up with some very specific projects/goals that PENTEX wants to accomplish. Select one of the subsidiaries to be responsible for doing it. Come up with an intermediary leader who can direct the project, but which is utterly expendable if the PCs just kill him. The PCs can then go about defeating that project/plan, yet PENTEX itself is still around. If the players don't feel that it seems like a win, be sure you somehow document the cost of their actions to PENTEX so they can see real money, power, assets, etc. be lost and not replaced. Perhaps mention a second future project that is now cancelled as a result of the losses from the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is similar to how it goes at our table. Pentex has so many fingers in so many pies that it's easy to come up with something to fight against, even if it's as simple as discovering that this thing that you're investigating that's caused by this local group has received help/financing/whatever from Pentex. That way, you have two baddies: Pentex, and the local source. It can be small, but so long as it's important to the characters, it FEELS big. Make sure there's a definitive and negative change or consequence if the baddies succeed. Make it something that will hurt the characters, even indirectly (actually, indirectly is often quite engaging because then you're taking the fight to them instead of the other way around). That way, when the characters win, it's a real victory. You may not have stopped Pentex, or even really hurt them all that much, but you've slowed their spread and you've stopped the local baddies. The key is making it all mean something to the players/characters despite the scale. That way, it's not just &quot;evil business of the week&quot; or &quot;of course it's Pentex AGAIN&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> Mix those goals and agendas up with non-Pentex goals and agendas, too, just to keep it fresh. One of our STs is excellent at dropping in hints and clues to another problem that's cropping up while we're in the midst of dealing with the one we're on. That way, we have to choose which is going to be the primary focus. Additionally, having a couple potential threats instead of just one goes a long way toward making the characters feel a little in over their heads, which can be great for an impending apocalypse setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:21:46-08:00","id":1023865,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> is absolutely right about what he wrote a couple of weeks ago.<br /> <br /> A group of Werewolves can always hunt down clues. This can start easily with a random encounter who have a vital letter with clear commands or note that scolds the random encounter monsters for being to weak that ends with the initials of the antagonist. This way they might be curious, but have only limited ways to find him. The longer the chronicle goes the more often they encounter notes, telephone calls or emails and always signed by the same Letters. If they achieve something spectacular give them a video where a person gives out vital commands. They think they have got the guy (and there are gifts to help to track them down people they have seen). As soon as they get to the guy in the video you dramatically reveal that the guy is just another underling. Pull a trick off that is similar to the maneuver that L used against Kira in the anime/movie/manga Death Note. A metallic changed voice will let them know that the main antagonist had foreseen a breach in communications and used this as a test. You can now communicate everything you want. Maybe the Antagonist says that he will stop for the foreseeable future in this region because they did destroy a huge part of his local power base. <br /> <br /> Antagonists retreat often, if they don't see a way to win. This will lead to them remember those initials even more, as they will most likely not believe him and they will be cautious, as he showed intelligence and cunning.<br /> <br /> Maybe the antagonist gives them information trying to destroy the pack or its relation with the Sept. Something like, along the lines that there is a traitor and as long as the traitor is there they won't be able to get to him anyway, as he knows what they are doing in the first place. They won't believe him, but they will be even more cautious and the other Garou will feel that.<br /> <br /> Another trick the antagonist can pull here is to insult them on a intellectual level. That they were not smart enough to catch him bla bla bla. Works often, but depends strongly on the people in your group. You can combine it by trying to stall time while important side characters are attacked and while they might insult him back they are wasting time which leads to pain and suffering. <br /> <br /> There are many things you can do, sometimes just &quot;borrow&quot; good antagonists from TV-Shows or movies that are ominous. The cigarette smoking man (just never reveal his face or name), L/Kira from deathnote or how Blofeld was sometimes handled in the Bond movies.<br /> The ominous ways are there to protect the big boss. If they names and faces where known someone would just assassinate them. Not only Garou but also competitors.<br /> <br /> All of this can be used, but it also can frustrate your players and you need to know how they feel about the chronicle. I did set something up that was quite similar in my last game, but because of frictions inside of the pack i shied away from using it. After all this is a game and sometimes easier chronicles are better for the group or take away spotlights from other areas of the game like pack discipline, order and Garou relationships. In the end, only the ST and the players know if this kind of antagonist will increase your roleplaying experience or hinders the group. We are not writing books, but have a interdependent relationship with our players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}